# Common Javadoc Tags

| Tag                      | Description                             |
| ------------------------ | --------------------------------------- |
| `@author`                | Specifies the author                    |
| `@version`               | Version of the class                    |
| `@param`                 | Describes a method parameter            |
| `@return`                | Describes the return value              |
| `@throws` / `@exception` | Describes exceptions thrown             |
| `@see`                   | Reference to related classes or methods |
| `@since`                 | Version when introduced                 |
| `@deprecated`            | Marks obsolete code                     |
| `{@link}`                | Creates clickable links                 |
| `{@code}`                | Displays code formatting                |
| `{@literal}`             | Displays text without interpreting HTML |

---

## Example Using Most Tags

```java
/**
 * Utility class for arithmetic operations.
 *
 * @author John
 * @version 2.0
 * @since Java 21
 */
public class Calculator {

    /**
     * Divides two integers.
     *
     * @param a Dividend
     * @param b Divisor
     * @return Quotient
     * @throws ArithmeticException if divisor is zero
     * @see Math
     */
    public int divide(int a, int b) {
        if (b == 0)
            throw new ArithmeticException("Cannot divide by zero");
        return a / b;
    }
}
```

